From: MacFinals
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: export syscall_log_current_wtid for the mac driver

Wine compiles the unix side with -fvisibility=hidden, and winemac.drv's .so links ntdll.so
directly, so only symbols explicitly marked visible resolve there (same mechanism as the
existing __attribute__((visibility("default"))) exports in loader.c, e.g. CW Hack 24067).

The C04 event-queue lock diagnostics (wine-macdrv-event-queue-lock.patch) call this from
cocoa_event.m to name the lock holder with the same Wine tid the syscall log uses; without
the export the winemac.drv link fails with "Undefined symbols: _syscall_log_current_wtid".
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -1516,6 +1516,7 @@
 
 /* C17: this thread's Windows tid for the fd-cache section owner record (server.c); 0 when the
  * thread has no slot (uncounted threads never block a dump reading either) */
+__attribute__((visibility("default")))
 UINT32 syscall_log_current_wtid(void)
 {
     if (syscall_log_my <= (void *)1) return 0;
